  "worked_solution": "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x-16}{{x}^{2}-6x+8} & =\\frac{8(x-2)}{(x-2)(x-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cancel{(x-2)}}{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\nx-4=0\\,\u27f9\\,x=4\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=4.$",
